@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] galileo-secret-custody
Marshall-injected credential values exist only inside per-request authorization
responses. They MUST NOT be persisted, logged, cached or exposed on any status
surface. GitHub transfer action headers and signed URLs MAY remain in bounded
ephemeral capability memory for at most sixty seconds under ADR-0198; they MUST
NOT enter durable storage, diagnostics, status surfaces or guest responses.
Guests can use integrations but never read their secrets.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] galileo-authority-boundary
Galileo MUST obtain current Marshall authorization before every upstream
effect and retain it through a bounded renewable lease while that effect is
open. Failed, invalid or late renewal MUST close the existing attempt without
retrying it. Guest headers cannot confer VM identity. Galileo MUST NOT access
Marshall's database.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] galileo-closed-routing
Guest input selects only the integration name, method and path. Generic target
origins, strip prefixes, injected headers and peer endpoints come exclusively
from the closed Marshall authorization response validated by the shared
protocol library. Built-in GitHub transfers MAY use only provider-issued,
shared-protocol-allowlisted targets held in execution-, generation- and
method-bound opaque capabilities. Fresh Marshall admission MUST precede every
capability use; guest URLs and headers MUST NOT select transfer authority.
